unting for 25 percent of the global  infections at that time  of those 12 million global infections  over 500 000 resulted in death  with over 130 000 fatalities occurring  in the united states accounting for 24  percent of the global covet 19 related  deaths  as of today just over three months later  the number of global infections has  grown from 12 million to over 38 million  with over 7.7 million confirmed cases in  the united states  and globally covet 19 has been the cause  of over 1 million deaths  with just over 213 000 deaths occurring  in the u.s  owing to the severe impact of this  disease throughout the world and the  high percentage  of morbidity and mortality it is of the  utmost importance to understand the  pathological mechanism of this disease  the causative agent of covid19 is sars  coronavirus 2 or sars cov2  a positive sense single stranded rna  virus and a beta coronavirus in the  family coronavira day  sars cov2 is one of seven human  pathogenic coronaviruses  whereas four of these pathogenic  coronaviruses typically cause  mild cold like symptoms the remaining  three pathogenic viruses sars covi  mers kobe and now sars covi2 can cause  severe disease  with sars covi and mers kobe resulting  in epidemics in 2003 and 2012  respectively  during infection sars cov2 enters into  host cells by both receptor mediated  entry  and receptor independent plasma membrane  fusion  during receptor mediated entry the viral  spike glycoprotein binds the angiotensin  converting enzyme 2  or ace2 receptor that is expressed on a  wide range of host cells  while sars cov also binds the ace2  receptor to facilitate entry and cause  disease  sars cov2 binds at a much higher  affinity  this increased affinity may play a part  in the increased infectivity and  worldwide spread of this novel virus  additionally the expression of the ace2  receptor on a wide variety of cell types  in multiple organ systems  may facilitate the systemic spread of  the virus in moderate to severe disease  sars cov2 can be transmitted both  directly and indirectly from an infected  host to a non-infected individual  unlike many respiratory viruses sars  cov2 can be transmitted from an infected  host even if they are asymptomatic or  pre-symptomatic  making it very difficult to discern if  any individual is contagious  in direct transmission an infected host  transmits the virus to a non-infected  individual directly  in the case of sars kobe 2 this is  mainly mediated by respiratory  transmission of large  short-range respiratory droplets these  virus-containing droplets are generated  when an infected individual sneezes  coughs  laughs sings or even talks  if a non-infected person is within range  of these infectious droplets  they can be exposed to the virus via  inhalation depositing infectious virus  into the upper and lower respiratory  tract  or even exposure via the mucosal  membranes of the eyes nose or mouth  the risk of direct transmission of stars  cov2 can be greatly reduced by following  social distancing guidelines  and properly wearing masks when in  public  indirect transmission of the virus  occurs when the virus is transmitted  from the infected host  to a susceptible individual indirectly  for sars cov2  this can occur via suspended small  particle long-range aerosols  or contamination of inanimate objects  termed fomites  while there has been controversy over  the aerosol transmission of stars kobe 2  the world health organization and  centers for disease control have updated  their guidance  stating that in indoor spaces with poor  ventilation small  particle infectious aerosols may remain  suspended and pose a greater  transmission risk than previously  thought  in the case of stars cov2 fomite or  vehicle transmission  could occur from infectious droplets  contaminating surfaces  such as doorknobs office equipment or  even the card reader at the cash  register  if a susceptible individual touches that  surface and then touches 